0..95 Comment "/// This source converts a call whose selected arm calls a definition at another call\'s result."
96..99 Comment "///"
100..201 Comment "/// It pins how the checker steps a call whose arm reaches `emp(tailOf(h))`, both calls stuck at `h`."
202..205 Comment "///"
206..460 Comment "/// The argument `tailOf(h)` is itself a call, so the arm reads back as a bind of that call ahead of the call it feeds. The checker steps the selecting call to the two calls, which convert with the same calls written out, and the kernel replays the step."
461..464 Comment "///"
465..481 Comment "/// - see: #3042"
482..498 Comment "/// - see: #2832"
